# Moxa ioThinx 45MR-2600.
# Converted automatically from the Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST); see ATTRIBUTION.md.
# Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation.
# Corrections are welcome (CONTRIBUTING.md). Remove @x_status once this table has been checked against the manual.
# | Moxa ioThinx 45MR-2600 — 16-channel DO (sink/NPN)
# | 
# | Source: ioThinx 4510 Series User's Manual V2.1, August 2019, Appendix A
# | Protocol: Modbus/TCP via ioThinx 4510 adapter, port 502
# | 
# | IMPORTANT: Addresses are MODULE-RELATIVE. Actual PDU address = slot_base + relative_address.
# | Slot base depends on which slot this module occupies in the ioThinx 4510 chassis.
# | Only ch0-3 support pulse output mode; ch4-15 are standard DO only.
# | 
# | FC01 (coil R/W): doStatus ch0-15 (16 BOOL, 0=OFF 1=ON),
# | doPulseStatus ch0-3 (4 BOOL, 0=Stop 1=Start)
# | FC02 (discrete input R): doMode ch0-15 (16 BOOL, 0=DO 1=Pulse)
# | FC03 (holding R/W): see [[registers]] below
# | FC04 (input R): doModeAll (1 WORD bitmask ch0-15)
@mbmap=1
@vendor=Moxa
@model=ioThinx 45MR-2600
@description=16-DO sink (NPN) output ioThinx 45MR slot module. Addresses are module-relative; actual PDU address = slot_base + relative_address. Only ch0-3 support pulse output mode; ch4-15 are DO-only. FC01: doStatus ch0-15 (0=OFF 1=ON), doPulseStatus ch0-3 (0=Stop 1=Start). FC02: doMode ch0-15 (0=DO 1=Pulse). FC03: doStatusAll bitmask (rel 0), doPulseCount ch0-3 u64 4-words/ch (rel 1-16), doPulseOnWidth ch0-3 (rel 17-20, unit 500us), doPulseOffWidth ch0-3 (rel 21-24, unit 500us), doPulseStatusAll bitmask (rel 25). FC04: doModeAll (1 WORD).
@source=Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST), modbus-library/moxa-iothinx-45mr-2600.toml; Source: ioThinx 4510 Series User's Manual V2.1, August 2019, Appendix A. Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation
@byte_order=ABCD
@address_base=0
@x_status=unverified
@x_origin=omniconsole

